          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The binary tetrahedral group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2T
            is, up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℍ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\mathbb{H}) \simeq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} SU(2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq Spin(3)
            of unit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            consisting of the 8 unit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm 1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm i
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ±
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm k
            and the 16 unit quaternions given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ε
                    %mn 0
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi ε
                    %mn 1
                  %mi i
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi ε
                    %mn 2
                  %mi j
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi ε
                    %mn 3
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac1{2}(\varepsilon_0 1 + \varepsilon_1 i + \varepsilon_2 j + \varepsilon_3 k)
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ε
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ε
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\varepsilon_0, \ldots, \varepsilon_3) \in \{-1, 1\}^4
          %p
            (These are also the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            that span the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/24-cell"} 24-cell
            as a convex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+polytope"} regular polytope
            in
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#basic_properties Basic properties
          %p
            The full tetrahedral group is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_4
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutations"} permutations
            of four elements (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://groupprops.subwiki.org/wiki/Full_tetrahedral_group_is_isomorphic_to_S4"} Full tetrahedral group is isomorphic to S4
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of
            = succeed "-preserving" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/alternating+group"} alternating group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_4
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+of+a+group"} group order
            is:
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo =
                  %mn 24
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert T_d\vert = 24
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo =
                  %mn 12
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert T\vert = 12
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mn 2
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo =
                  %mn 24
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert 2T\vert = 24
          #QuaternionSubgroup.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion+group"} quaternion group
                inside
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+tetrahedral+group"} binary tetrahedral group
            %p
              The binary tetrahedral group contains the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion+group"} quaternion group
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order"} order
              8, hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+dihedral+group"} binary dihedral group
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+of+a+group"} order
              8, as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+subgroup"} normal subgroup
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 4
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mn 8
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mn 2
                    %mi T
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    2 D_4 =Q_8 \subset 2 T
                    \\,.
            %p
              In fact the only
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroups+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroups of SU(2)
              which contain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 4
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 D_4 =Q_8
              as a proper subgroup are the exceptional ones, hence the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+tetrahedral+group"} binary tetrahedral group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+octahedral+group"} binary octahedral group
              and the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+icosahedral+group"} binary icosahedral group
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "quaternion+group#InclusionInLargerFininteSubgroupsOfSU2"} this Prop
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion+group"} quaternion group
