          %h3#group_cohomology Group cohomology
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            of the tetrahedral group is discussed in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Groupprops"} Groupprops
            %a{:href => "#TomodaZvengrowski08"} Tomoda &amp; Zvengrowski 08, Sec. 4.1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kirdar13"} Kirdar 13
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#EpaGanter16"} Epa &amp; Ganter 16, p. 12
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GL%282%2C3%29"} GL(2,3)
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classification+of+finite+rotation+groups"} classification of finite rotation groups
            goes back to:
          %ul
            %li#Klein1884
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Klein"}> Felix Klein
              , chapter I.4 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Vorlesungen über das Ikosaeder und die Auflösung der Gleichungen vom fünften Grade
              %em Lectures on the Icosahedron and the Resolution of Equations of Degree Five
              by George Morrice 1888,
              %a{:href => "https://archive.org/details/cu31924059413439"} online version
          %p Exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              Tony Phillips,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~tony/bintet/"} The Geometry of the Binary Tetrahedral Group in SU(2)
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tetrahedral_symmetry"} Tetrahedral symmetry
          %p
            Discussion of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
          %ul
            %li#TomodaZvengrowski08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Satoshi+Tomoda"}> Satoshi Tomoda
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Zvengrowski"} Peter Zvengrowski
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Remarks on the cohomology of finite fundamental groups of 3-manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.1876"} arXiv:0904.1876
            %li#Kirdar13
              %p
                Mehmet Kirdar,
                %em On The K-Ring of the Classifying Space of the Symmetric Group on Four Letters
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1309.4238"}> arXiv:1309.4238
                )
            %li#Groupprops
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Groupprops"}> Groupprops
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://groupprops.subwiki.org/wiki/Group_cohomology_of_symmetric_group:S4"} Group cohomology of symmetric group:S4
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+central+extension"} higher central extension
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Platonic+2-groups"} Platonic 2-groups
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Epa10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narthana+Epa"}> Narthana Epa
